<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sesia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sesia is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, about 138 km long, rising on the glaciers of Monte Rosa and flowing south through the Valsesia past Vercelli to join the Po. Its plain, irrigated by canals, is a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing area, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it lay between the territories of Vercelli and Novara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sesia.jpg" alt="Sesia" width="300" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utente:Fotogian · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sesia.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
